{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1792","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"E. Divisors and Table"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2.5 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You are given an $$$n \\times n$$$ multiplication table and a positive integer $$$m = m_1 \\cdot m_2$$$. A $$$n \\times n$$$ multiplication table is a table with $$$n$$$ rows and $$$n$$$ columns numbered from $$$1$$$ to $$$n$$$, where $$$a_{i, j} = i \\cdot j$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each divisor $$$d$$$ of $$$m$$$, check: does $$$d$$$ occur in the table at least once, and if it does, what is the "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"minimum"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" row that contains $$$d$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains a single integer $$$t$$$ ($$$1 \\le t \\le 10$$$) — the number of test cases."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first and only line of each test case contains three integers $$$n$$$, $$$m_1$$$ and $$$m_2$$$ ($$$1 \\le n \\le 10^9$$$; $$$1 \\le m_1, m_2 \\le 10^9$$$) — the size of the multiplication table and the integer $$$m$$$ represented as $$$m_1 \\cdot m_2$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each test case, let $$$d_1, d_2, \\dots, d_k$$$ be "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"all"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" divisors of $$$m$$$ sorted in the increasing order. And let $$$a_1, a_2, \\dots, a_k$$$ be an array of answers, where $$$a_i$$$ is equal to the minimum row index where divisor $$$d_i$$$ occurs, or $$$0$$$, if there is no such row."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Since array $$$a$$$ may be large, first, print an integer $$$s$$$ — the number of divisors of $$$m$$$ that "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"are present"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" in the $$$n \\times n$$$ table. Next, print a single value $$$X = a_1 \\oplus a_2 \\oplus \\dots \\oplus a_k$$$, where $$$\\oplus$$$ denotes the "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bitwise_operation#XOR"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"bitwise XOR operation"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n3\n3 72 1\n10 10 15\n6 1 210\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n6 2\n10 0\n8 5\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first test case, $$$m = 72 \\cdot 1 = 72$$$ and has $$$12$$$ divisors $$$[1, 2, 3, 4, 6, 8, 9, 12, 18, 24, 36, 72]$$$. The $$$3 \\times 3$$$ multiplication table looks like that:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"attrs":{"header":false},"kind":"table_cell"},{"attrs":{"header":false},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1"}],"kind":"table_cell"},{"attrs":{"header":false},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"2"}],"kind":"table_cell"},{"attrs":{"header":false},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"3"}],"kind":"table_cell"}],"kind":"table_row"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"header":false},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1"}],"kind":"table_cell"},{"attrs":{"header":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"table_cell"},{"attrs":{"header":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"2"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"table_cell"},{"attrs":{"header":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"3"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"table_cell"}],"kind":"table_row"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"header":false},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"2"}],"kind":"table_cell"},{"attrs":{"header":false},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"2"}],"kind":"table_cell"},{"attrs":{"header":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"4"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"table_cell"},{"attrs":{"header":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"6"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"table_cell"}],"kind":"table_row"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"header":false},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"3"}],"kind":"table_cell"},{"attrs":{"header":false},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"3"}],"kind":"table_cell"},{"attrs":{"header":false},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"6"}],"kind":"table_cell"},{"attrs":{"header":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"9"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"table_cell"}],"kind":"table_row"}],"kind":"table_body"}],"kind":"table"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each divisor of $$$m$$$ that is present in the table, the position with minimum row index is marked. So the array of answers $$$a$$$ is equal to $$$[1, 1, 1, 2, 2, 0, 3, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0]$$$. There are only $$$6$$$ non-zero values, and xor of $$$a$$$ is equal to $$$2$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second test case, $$$m = 10 \\cdot 15 = 150$$$ and has $$$12$$$ divisors $$$[1, 2, 3, 5, 6, 10, 15, 25, 30, 50, 75, 150]$$$. All divisors except $$$75$$$ and $$$150$$$ are present in the $$$10 \\times 10$$$ table. Array $$$a$$$ $$$=$$$ $$$[1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 3, 5, 3, 5, 0, 0]$$$. There are $$$10$$$ non-zero values, and xor of $$$a$$$ is equal to $$$0$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the third test case, $$$m = 1 \\cdot 210 = 210$$$ and has $$$16$$$ divisors $$$[1, 2, 3, 5, 6, 7, 10, 14, 15, 21, 30, 35, 42, 70, 105, 210]$$$. The $$$6 \\times 6$$$ table with marked divisors is shown below:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"attrs":{"header":false},"kind":"table_cell"},{"attrs":{"header":false},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1"}],"kind":"table_cell"},{"attrs":{"header":false},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"2"}],"kind":"table_cell"},{"attrs":{"header":false},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"3"}],"kind":"table_cell"},{"attrs":{"header":false},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"4"}],"kind":"table_cell"},{"attrs":{"header":false},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"5"}],"kind":"table_cell"},{"attrs":{"header":false},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"6"}],"kind":"table_cell"}],"kind":"table_row"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"header":false},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1"}],"kind":"table_cell"},{"attrs":{"header":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"table_cell"},{"attrs":{"header":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"2"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"table_cell"},{"attrs":{"header":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"3"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"tabl